-- title:
--   Level automorphisms for Γ₀(M') at q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $q\ell$, and let $\xi \in L$ be a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity. Put $N_0 = (q\ell)^2 M'$ and let $H =$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) $(q\ell)\,M'$ be the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/N_0)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((X))$ (Laurent series over $L$) assumed equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) $N_0\,H$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, that is, the $L$-subfield of $L((X))$ generated by the image of that field under the coefficientwise embedding $\mathbb{Q}((X)) \to L((X))$. The assertion is: for every $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$ there exists an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) N₀ H γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29), i.e.: for every weight $k \in \mathbb{Z}$, every pair of modular forms $f, g$ of weight $k$ on the subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}(2,\mathbb{R})$ attached to [`CohCarrier.GammaH`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) $N_0\,H$, every pair of power series $p_f, p_g$ over $\mathbb{Z}$ whose images in $\mathbb{C}[[X]]$ are the $q$-expansions of $f$ and $g$ with the rational Laurent series attached to $p_g$ nonzero, every $x \in K$ whose image in $L((X))$ is the coefficientwise image of the quotient of the rational Laurent series of $p_f$ by that of $p_g$, and every ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$, the coefficientwise image under $\iota$ of $\tau(x)$ times the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k$ `conjElemN` $(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1}$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k$ `conjElemN` $(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1}$, where `conjElemN` $m\,\delta$ denotes the determinant-one real matrix $\begin{pmatrix} a & b/m \\ mc & d\end{pmatrix}$ attached to $\delta = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d\end{pmatrix}$.
--
--   This is the $q = 2$ case of the existence of the automorphism of the base-changed function field of $X_H((q\ell)^2M')$ induced by an element of $\Gamma_0(M')$, characterised through its effect on quotients of modular forms with integral $q$-expansions after conjugation by $\mathrm{diag}(q\ell,1)$. It feeds the determination of the group of such level automorphisms and the description of the fixed field inside the base-changed Laurent series field used on the full-level leg of the argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_AuxLevel_exists_isLevelAutAt_of_mem_gamma0_of_eq_two.lean

